<title>FRANCE: Bouygues Offshore wins Hungary contract.</title>
<headline>Bouygues Offshore wins Hungary contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Energy services firm Bouygues Offshore said on Monday it had won an $86.5 million contract to build oil storage tanks for the Crude Storage Company of Hungary.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore will share the contract with the parent Bouygues construction group through a 50/50 joint venture, the company said in a statement. Bouygues owns 60 percent of Bouygues Offshore.</p>
<p>The contract is for six storage tanks, each with capacity for 80,000 cubic metres, with delivery of the last tank at the end of 1998.</p>
</text>
